Here are the step-by-step instructions to set up a full local production-like pipeline for:

📄 PDF → Text → Embedding → Qdrant Vector DB

Using:

Ollama (nomic-embed-text)

Qdrant (via Docker)

Node.js script to handle PDF parsing, embedding, and storing

✅ 1. Install Requirements
🧠 Ollama (for Embedding)
bash
Copy
Edit
curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh
ollama run nomic-embed-text
This downloads the nomic-embed-text model and starts the local API at http://localhost:11434.

📦 Qdrant (Vector DB)
Option A: Docker (Recommended)
bash
Copy
Edit
docker run -d \
  -p 6333:6333 \
  -p 6334:6334 \
  --name qdrant \
  qdrant/qdrant
Qdrant will now be running at:

REST API → http://localhost:6333

Web UI → http://localhost:6333/dashboard (optional with Qdrant Cloud)

✅ 2. Project Setup
bash
Copy
Edit
mkdir llm-pipeline && cd llm-pipeline
npm init -y
npm install pdf-parse axios gpt-3-encoder uuid
Optional: Add .env and config separation later for production.

